OL,3,GNEWSAWhy London's dry ground will be
OL,4,Aslow to recover
OL,5,
OL,6,FLondon is still experiencing drought
OL,7,Fconditions and, despite recent rain,
OL,8,Fmuch of the capital's ground will take
OL,9,Ftime to recover after weeks of
OL,10,Frecord-breaking dry weather.
OL,12,FAbout 80% of London sits on clay, which
OL,13,Fextends to depths of more than 100m
OL,14,F(328ft) in some places.
OL,16,FThe clay has lost moisture, causing it
OL,17,Fto shrink and crack. In some cases,
OL,18,Fthis can lead to subsidence, resulting
OL,19,Fin damage to buildings and homes.
OL,23,APub: 30-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,325,320,200,140,0,100
